    description: "Overview: Does it feel like your motor is a little wound up? Time for a makeover! Motors are everywhere, from appliances to toothbrushes to tools. Just about anything that uses electricity and moves. This exploration takes a look inside them to see how they work and experiment with making a more powerful one. And it's going to look great. - What: Motor Makeover - When: Oh, it's time. - Concepts: electromagnetism, physics, cir…\n\nMaterials:\n- See full materials list on the activity page.\n\nBuild Steps:\n1. Test Your Motor - Let's see how this puppy runs!\n2. Inside Out - Time to pop it open.\n3. Motor Anatomy - Starting from the metal tabs, the first stop is at the brushes.\n4. Make a Base - Raise your motor to the sky!\n5. Make a Motor - Here's the fun part!\n\nLearning Focus: motors, electronics, electricity, electromagnetism, magnets, takeapart\nOriginal Activity: https://www.instructables.com/Motor-Makeover/",
