    title: "Balloon Trombone",
    summary: "This is the trombone for those that can't afford the brass.",
    description: "Overview: This is the trombone for those that can't afford the brass. It also works great for the straw enthusiast, scientists of sound, arts-and-crafts-drawer musicians, and budding clowns. There's something great about making your own instrument, as you can see all the parts that come together to affect sound. In making this, you get membranes, vibration, resonance, and variables to adjust that all go into making a sound th…\n\nMaterials:\n- See full materials list on the activity page.\n\nBuild Steps:\n1. Make a Membrane - Every good wind instrument works by something wiggling back and forth.\n2. Mold a Mouthpiece - You'll be making sweet (well, not so sweet) music in no time!\n3. Cap With a Straw - Press on the PVC end cap on the side opposite the balloon.\n4. Add a Support and Slide - Take your second length of cut flexi-straw and slide it into the other.\n5. Trombone Like a Champion - Well it's not going to play itself.\n\nLearning Focus: science, sound, resonance, physics, wavelength, frequency\nOriginal Activity: https://www.instructables.com/Balloon-Trombone/",
