    summary: "This takes some shake to make!",
    description: "Overview: This takes some shake to make! Time to make some light with the original shake weight, the piston generator. No batteries needed! Just some good old fashioned human power. This is one of my favorites for an introduction to electro-magnetism, and works great in concert with showing that electricity can make a magnet. Now you know it works the other way, too. - What: Shake Generator - Concepts: electromagnetism, polar…\n\nMaterials:\n- See full materials list on the activity page.\n\nBuild Steps:\n1. Wrap It! - Let's get into the loop.\n2. When Two LEDs Become One - What a pair!\n3. Solder to Your Wire - Take the two pairs of legs, and solder one to each end of the wire where the insulation has been stripped away.\n4. Magnets in the Chamber - Put your magnet or magnets into the tube, and get ready to rock.\n5. Make LIGHT! - Shake to make!\n\nLearning Focus: generator, electronics, electomagnetism, magnet, motor, led\nOriginal Activity: https://www.instructables.com/Shake-Generator/",
