    summary: "Time to get lost in a project!",
    description: "Overview: Time to get lost in a project! The Everchanging Ball Maze is a handheld 3D puzzle that is never the same twice. Put it together with some geometry and puzzle-making skills, and solve it using sound, touch, and memory. I like it because it allows students and teachers to make quick, light-hearted challenges for each other which sometimes can be quick and sometimes devastatingly difficult. GET A-MAZE-D. What: Everchan…\n\nMaterials:\n- See full materials list on the activity page.\n\nBuild Steps:\n1. Start and Finish - We need a beginning an end!\n2. Drilling and Filling - Let's put the start and finish in some end caps.\n3. Make Tunnels - The main path of your ball maze is going to be PVC tubes.\n4. Assemble a Puzzle - Start putting together your first ball maze for someone to figure out.\n5. Get A-MAZE-D - Time to hop in your labyrinth or give it to a friend!\n6. Re-Make, Re-Maze! - After you've done a maze, make another for a friend!\n\nLearning Focus: puzzle, labyrinth, plexus, 3d, changing, shifting\nOriginal Activity: https://www.instructables.com/Everchanging-Ball-Maze/",
