    title: "Heart Dissection",
    summary: "Have a heart!",
    description: "Overview: Have a heart! The original pump that is the drumbeat of our lives is an amazing structure. You've seen them on holiday cards, but now it's time for the real thing. A heart dissection is a fascinating experience that is at the core of our circulatory system, and our body as a whole. There our other dissection photos out there, but I wanted to make a clear walkthrough for teachers and students who are doing it. What:…\n\nMaterials:\n- See full materials list on the activity page.\n\nBuild Steps:\n1. Feel the Beat - Check to see if those tickers are ticking!\n2. Check for Blood - Sure we've been told we're full of blood, but how do we know?\n3. Have a Heart - Starting with a pig heart, there is a lot to notice before we start cutting.\n4. Veins and Arteries - How many tubes go into and out of the heart?\n5. Making the Cut - There are many ways you can cut your heart, but the most informative will perhaps be directly down the interventricular sulcus.\n6. A Four Bedroom House - The first thing to look for are the four rooms of the heart.\n7. The Pieces of the Heart - There are many things to look and learn about inside the heart.\n8. Keep Exploring - There's more inside the heart alone, and more to see when you compare them.\n\nLearning Focus: heart, anatomy, biology, science, school, classroom\nOriginal Activity: https://www.instructables.com/Heart-Dissection/",
