    description: "Overview: HOOOOOONK! Can you hear that mellifluous tone? But no, it's not an entire flock of hyped up ducks, it's the most marvelous honk! This is an introduction project to the way that single reed instruments work and sound resonance as well. All while sounding like a wily waterfowl. Let's quack it up. - What: The Most Marvelous Honk - Why: valid question - Concepts: sound, resonance, music, single-reed instruments, vibrati…\n\nMaterials:\n- See full materials list on the activity page.\n\nBuild Steps:\n1. The Sound - The most marvelous mouthpiece sounds amazingly...like your standard duck.\n2. Make a Diagonal Cut - Start with your short piece of PVC and make a diagonal cut, around 30 degrees or so.\n3. Cut and Attach Your Reed - Oh we're so close to annoying everyone!\n4. Let Ducks Ring - To play your most marvelous mouthpiece, cup your lips around both sides, and you can use your teeth to stabilize.\n\nLearning Focus: honk, instrument, resonance, single reed, saxophone, clarinet\nOriginal Activity: https://www.instructables.com/The-Most-Marvelous-Honk/",
