    description: "Overview: Well ahoy! You've set sail for the seven seas, and your barge has just bumped into a beautiful bay. It's your dream island of course! This is a project to make, model, and map out your landscape involving everything from math to art to science. It is also a great way to learn how to make and read topographical maps. Got that cabin fever? Let's go! - What: Dream Island Mapping Project - Where: your dreams - Concepts:…\n\nMaterials:\n- See full materials list on the activity page.\n\nBuild Steps:\n1. Mold Your Island - Time to speed up some earth processes!\n2. Take Topo Readings - This is an easy way to learn how to make and read topographical maps!\n3. Make Altitude Profile - Once you have it all mapped out, transfer your map to paper by holding up paper and plastic to glass or a lightbox.\n4. Lay Out Your Island - Dream some schemes!\n5. Make Trails or Roads - Let's get moving.\n6. Measure Your Peaks and Coastline - When geologists and surveyors are looking at new land, they often look at the extremes.\n7. Estimate Total Area - How big is your island?\n8. Keep Going! - Oh there's no limits to what to be done with an island.\n\nLearning Focus: map, mapping, cartography, island, topo, topographical\nOriginal Activity: https://www.instructables.com/Dream-Island-Mapping-Project/",
