    summary: "On your marks, get set, stay put!",
    description: "Overview: On your marks, get set, stay put! Have you ever that get up and not-go feeling? Well this car feels it, too. With a fan in the front and a sail in the back, you'd think it would be the perfect self-contained contraption. After all, it's a sail car that can make it's own wind, right? It wants to go everywhere, but ends up going nowhere. The self-defeating fan car is one of my favorite contraptions, and it has a secre…\n\nMaterials:\n- See full materials list on the activity page.\n\nBuild Steps:\n1. Make a Car Chassis - Time to choose a shape to your hot rod (or rather not-rod)!\n2. Mount Electronics - Throw on a healthy dose of hot glue on your motor, and stick it to your support.\n3. The Fan: Two Options! - I know, you do these projects for the fans.\n4. Host the Sail! - Let's add a catcher of the wind.\n5. Straws and Axles - It's time to work on the car's underbelly.\n6. Wheel Up - Your car is going to need some stunning wheels.\n7. Self-Defeating Car Vs. Self-Successful Car - Turn your fan on, and as the wind catches in the sails, watch as your car......goes nowhere.\n\nLearning Focus: fan car, sail car, diy car, motor, turbine, wind power\nOriginal Activity: https://www.instructables.com/Self-Defeating-Fan-Car/",
