    title: "Oil and Ice Density Experiment",
    summary: "Oil and Water.",
    description: "Overview: Oil and Water. Plaid and Argyle. Hulk Hogan and a movie acting career. Some things just don't mix. In science, we can use these things to experiment with things such as density, buoyancy, and other physical properties. Oil and Water have been played with for a long time, but amazing things happen when you add ice to the mix! This experiment is a quickie and easy to make, but a great way to increase the complexity of…\n\nMaterials:\n- See full materials list on the activity page.\n\nBuild Steps:\n1. Make Blue Ice Cubes - If you like clear ice cubes, you're going to love blue ones!\n2. Add Oil and Cubes - When you're ready for the experiment, add vegetable oil to a cup, and then gently place an ice cube in the top.\n3. Watch Your Experiment in Action! - The amazing part of this experiment happens as you let the ice cube melt.\n4. Going Further - You can take this experiment further, and I'm excited to see how you go about it!\n\nLearning Focus: mixing oil and water, density, buoyancy, physics, learning, education\nOriginal Activity: https://www.instructables.com/Oil-and-Ice-Density-Experiment/",
