    summary: "Sure zombies may love eating brains, but what will you serve them to drink?",
    description: "Overview: Sure zombies may love eating brains, but what will you serve them to drink? Hosting the undead just got a lot easier with Zombie Sodas! You won't just survive the zombie apocalypse, but enjoy it, too. These are great for your regular mortal friends and kids as well. I love making these, and it's a super easy way to carbonate a beverage and send a glove flying across the room at the same time. It also doubles as an a…\n\nMaterials:\n- Plastic Cups (wide-rim, SOLO work well)\n- Straws (thin elbow straws are great)\n- Dry Ice\n- Nitrile Gloves (latex also works, but watch out for allergies)\n- Juice (orange, lemonade, apple, POG, anything!)\n\nBuild Steps:\n1. Mix Your Juices - To each their own!\n2. Throw in a Dry Ice Chunk - Break up your dry ice with a hammer, or just slap the bag against a table.\n3. Top Off With a Glove - Zombie time!\n4. Mmmmm....Zombie Soda! - To keep it safe, place a skinny elbow straw in and enjoy the sweet nectar of the undead.\n\nLearning Focus: zombie, soda, haunt, halloween, dry ice, carbonation\nOriginal Activity: https://www.instructables.com/Zombie-Soda/",
