    title: "Liquid Hourglass",
    summary: "It's 2:59pm.",
    description: "Overview: It's 2:59pm. The school bell rings in one minute. The teacher is going off about something like \"viscosity\" or \"density\" or some other made-up word, but has still forgotten to assign homework. There's a chance you might get off free to build tree forts all weekend long with Jamico. You look at the wall for the clock. It's missing. It has been replaced by a weird double-bottle piece of trash thing. Time has slowed do…\n\nMaterials:\n- See full materials list on the activity page.\n\nBuild Steps:\n1. Gather Materials - Time to get your act together.\n2. Prep Your Bottles - A nice easy warm-up!\n3. Join the Caps - Use some strong glue (epoxy or super) to glue the heads of the caps together (twins!) Hold in position until solid, and then duct tape around the rim…\n4. Insert Straws - Use a pair of scissors to make two straw-diameter holes in your bottle caps that go all the way through.\n5. Fill 'Em Up! - It's time for the liquids, and the potential for major oil spills!\n6. Attach the Bottles - Here's the great sleight of hand moment.\n7. Hourglass Drops! - You've done it!\n\nLearning Focus: viscosity, pressure, density, liquid, fluid, physics\nOriginal Activity: https://www.instructables.com/Liquid-Hourglass/",
