    subject: "STEAM Activity",
    title: "Water Drop Science: 8 Explorations",
    summary: "Water you waiting for?",
    description: "Overview: Water you waiting for? There's an ocean of knowledge and experience lying in every wee drop water, and it's now you can start checking it out. From looking at surface tension to magnifying effects to vapor cushions, the water drop makes being little seem like a pretty big deal. I love doing these explorations with my students, and each one is a take-off point for more. Water Drop Science: 8 Explorations is a way to…\n\nMaterials:\n- See full materials list on the activity page.\n\nBuild Steps:\n1. Leidenfrost Drops - A hot drop on the right surface will start to boogie.\n2. Water Lenses - Drop a few water drops on to a mirror to get a fascinating lens effect looking back at you.\n3. Penny Blobs (surface Tension) - See how big you can make your penny blobs before they spill over (44 drops for one of them!).\n4. Water Drop Macro Lens - With a dab of water on your phone's camera, you can suddenly create a macro lens for some up-close magnifying photography.\n5. Life in a Drop - A drop of water can be like a little world when it comes to microfauna.\n6. Accordian Snake (capillary Action) - This one is a fast-food special.\n7. Drops on Leaves - See how nature deals with the wet stuff!\n8. Water Drop Trampoline - With a little bit of laminar air flow, you can get water drops to hop around!\n\nLearning Focus: water, drop, science, raindrop, classroom, education\nOriginal Activity: https://www.instructables.com/Water-Drop-Science-8-Explorations/",
