    title: "Side-Bending Goggles",
    summary: "The world is not as you see it.",
    description: "Overview: The world is not as you see it. Particularly when you're sporting light-bending, orientation-ending, lenses that make even the most eagle-eyed among us go out of whack. With these side-bending goggles, the world appears a little more to the left than it really is. And it's all with just a bit of acrylic rod, frames, some hot glue, and a healthy dose of optical physics. This is a great tool for (a) ridiculous silline…\n\nMaterials:\n- See full materials list on the activity page.\n\nBuild Steps:\n1. Optics and Refraction - Our obsession with light is clear.\n2. Cut Your Acrylic - Set up your acrylic rod with your saw!\n3. Sand Those Lenses - To get acrylic base to transparent takes a bit of work.\n4. Buff and Polish - Time to get buff(ed)!\n5. Glue Those Glasses - Pop out the regular old boring frames of your classes, and replace with awesome ones!\n6. Bend That Light! - With your vision bent sideways, try to do everyday things!\n\nLearning Focus: optics, light, bend, refraction, physics, classroom\nOriginal Activity: https://www.instructables.com/Side-Bending-Goggles/",
