    title: "Lava Boogers! (aka Waxy Earth Science)",
    summary: "What happens when a volcano has a runny nose?",
    description: "Overview: What happens when a volcano has a runny nose? Slightly more powerful than your average human flu, it usually involves a whole lot ash, acid rain, mudslides, and some fiery lava flow. That's right, good old fashioned fun! If you want to learn about the creation of igneous rock, but don't own explosive volcano homeowner's insurance, you may want to try this waxy option instead! With a little Crayola crafting, we can g…\n\nMaterials:\n- See full materials list on the activity page.\n\nBuild Steps:\n1. Weathering Your Crayons - Pick some raw minerals (crayons) out of the box, and combine your favorite colors.\n2. Sedimentary Crayon! - First stop on our rock cycle is sedimentary rock, which is the accumulation of sediment and minerals mixed and deposited in water, and slowly become…\n3. Metamorphic Crayon! - Metamorphic rock is the happy layover between sedimentary and igneous rock.\n4. Igneous Crayon! - Time to make some boogers.\n5. You've Got Lava Boogers! - Oh man!\n\nLearning Focus: earth science, geology, rock cycle, igneous, sedimentary, metamorphic\nOriginal Activity: https://www.instructables.com/Lava-Boogers-waxy-Earth-Science/",
