    title: "Grow Seeds Without Soil!",
    summary: "Oh the places they'll grow!",
    description: "Overview: Oh the places they'll grow! Whether you want to eat them, grow them, or throw them in a maraca, seeds are nature's suitcases of magic. From the smallest orchid seed at 1/35,000,000th of an ounce to the largest coconut seed at just under forty pounds, seeds are food, culture, and ultimately, life. So let's grow some, yah? If you want to check out seeds in action with a classroom or at home, you don't even need soil t…\n\nMaterials:\n- See full materials list on the activity page.\n\nBuild Steps:\n1. Soak Your Paper - Give your paper towel a quick dip so that it is moist throughout but not soaking.\n2. Tuck in Your Seeds - Fold your seeds in to the paper towel, so that they have a little space between them.\n3. Bottle It Up and Place! - Take your folded up seeds and put them into a bottle, and close the cap.\n4. Unveil Your Seeds! - So simple!\n\nLearning Focus: biology, seeds, plant life, life cycle, germinate, gardener\nOriginal Activity: https://www.instructables.com/Start-Seeds-Without-Soil/",
