    schoolName: "Instructables Educator Collection",
    grade: "6-10",
    subject: "STEAM Activity",
    title: "Grow Bacteria From Gross Stuff!",
    summary: "Ever had that hankering to grow millions of something?",
    description: "Overview: Ever had that hankering to grow millions of something? With a little swab from the inside of your mouth or the back of a toilet seat, you'll have a veritable bacteria farm empire in no time at all. Ever wanted to prove that a dog's mouth is cleaner than Ted from accounting's desk? Now is the time to do it with science! Making agar agar plates for bacteria is a great way to (1) Grow and learn about the microorganisms…\n\nMaterials:\n- See full materials list on the activity page.\n\nBuild Steps:\n1. Mark Your Dish - Start off easy by dividing your petri dish in to several quadrants where we'll test different swabs.\n2. The Bacteria Food Mix - Time to make something the bacteria culture we'll be talking about for weeks!\n3. Pour and Refrigerate - Pour your food mix into the bottom of your petri dish so it is about 1/4\" or so deep.\n4. Swab the Decks! - Time to get gross!\n5. Replace Lid and Tape - Cap your petri dish and you can add some tape to keep the lid on while we wait for our bacteria colonies to grow.\n6. Bacteria TA-DAAAA!!!! (and More) - After only a couple of days, colonies will start to grow and grow and grow.\n\nLearning Focus: bacteria plates, agar agar, petri dish, grow, culture, microorganisms\nOriginal Activity: https://www.instructables.com/Growing-Bacteria-From-Gross-Stuff/",
    challenge: "Build and demonstrate \"Grow Bacteria From Gross Stuff!\" while explaining the key ideas behind bacteria plates, agar agar, petri dish.",
    solution: "Follow the guided activity flow, prototype quickly, test performance, and iterate until the build works reliably.",
