    summary: "Got that tickle for a pickle, but feeling fickle about the wait?",
    description: "Overview: Got that tickle for a pickle, but feeling fickle about the wait? With your hand-powered vacuum, you can convert your cucumbers in about 30 seconds to delectable dills of delight! This pickling relies on a fascinating process using negative pressure to collapse the cell walls of your cucumber, and break down the membranes, letting water out, and your vinegar brine in. Whether you're in it for the science or in it for…\n\nMaterials:\n- See full materials list on the activity page.\n\nBuild Steps:\n1. Mix Your Brine - Flavors and preferences will vary here, but for the most part, you'll want to start off with pouring in some vinegar.\n2. Cut and Load Your Cucumber - For instant-pickling, thin slices work best.\n3. Pickle Time! - With your cucumbers in the syringe, pull enough of your brine to submerge them.\n4. Hold for 30 Seconds (also Science Time!) - As you hold the vacuum for 30 seconds, you can take a moment to check out the science.\n5. Extract Ze Pickles and Enjoy! - Push out your brine into your cup, remove the plunger, and pour out your pickles!\n\nLearning Focus: pickle, vacuum, air pressure, infusion, diffiusion, pickling\nOriginal Activity: https://www.instructables.com/Instant-Pickles-30-second-vacuum-pickles/",
