    title: "Cardboard Fortress Battle! (capture the Flag)",
    summary: "Hold thine cardboard horses, and raise thouest cardboard tubes, because ye have been called upon for delightful papery battle!",
    description: "Overview: Hold thine cardboard horses, and raise thouest cardboard tubes, because ye have been called upon for delightful papery battle! When you mix forts, cardboard, and capture the flag, you're sure to get something great! Whether you're a full-on LARPer or allergic to the idea of going to a Medieval Times restaurant, you'll still enjoy this a bunch. Time to lay siege to your recycling bins, and get ready to add some glory…\n\nMaterials:\n- See full materials list on the activity page.\n\nBuild Steps:\n1. Assemble the Cardboard Hoard - Time to get out collecting!\n2. Shields and Sword Handles - Measure your tubes to see how wide they are, and make a handle with a hole accordingly.\n3. Load Up! - Throw all that stuff in a car along with some markers, flags, tape, and a boombox, and you're ready to go find your friends!\n4. Forging Swords - No sweat!\n5. Smithing Shields - Making a shield is a wee more tricky than swords, but not bad.\n6. Rules of Engagement - So while it's super fun to just whack each other with cardboard, here are some rules as a framework for how to whack each other with cardboard and st…\n7. Building the Fortresses - As stated in the rules, each team gets five minutes to build their forts with the flag somewhere inside.\n8. Speeches From Generals - Every battle needs some epic speeches.\n9. Battle for Honor! - Oh, the epicness of it all.\n\nLearning Focus: cardboard, battle, sword, shield, capture the flag, play\nOriginal Activity: https://www.instructables.com/Cardboard-Fortress-Battle-capture-the-flag/",
