    summary: "For those that travel on a path slightly more gooey.",
    description: "Overview: For those that travel on a path slightly more gooey. Viscosity! It's the stickiness of life that keeps everything from lava to jelly in check. With the viscosity tube tumbler, you can look at everything from air bubble races to density columns to sedimentation in real time. Grab your glitter, your honey, oil, alcohol, your dirt, your sand, and let's go on a viscous and dense ride. This is great for any home, museum,…\n\nMaterials:\n- See full materials list on the activity page.\n\nBuild Steps:\n1. Leakiness Check! - All righty!\n2. The Tube Holder - This is like a giant test tube holder.\n3. Two End Circles - These are going to be what attach to your tube holder.\n4. Screw Together - Time to make a wooden barbell.\n5. Side Supports - These will hold your spinning contraption in the air.\n6. The Other Side of the Lazy Susan - This is the trickiest step!\n7. The Wood Base - Choose a wood base from a board a little larger than your contraption.\n8. Tube Time! - We're now going to make something to hold the tubes in place.\n9. End Caps - Add end caps to one side of each tube.\n\nLearning Focus: viscosity, density, science, education, classroom, school\nOriginal Activity: https://www.instructables.com/Viscosity-Tube-Tumbler/",
