    description: "Overview: Whether you want to wind down or wind up, this tube is soon to be your favorite automatic aerodynamic magic. Like the giant bubble fan from Willy Wonka's factory, this easy to make wind tube is great for exploring what flies, spins, tumbles, soars and falls, all easily mobile for the teacher/parent/adult/kiddo on the go. There are other tubes out there in the world, and this one is inspired by this one at the Explor…\n\nMaterials:\n- See full materials list on the activity page.\n\nBuild Steps:\n1. Materials Notes - Yay!\n2. The Wood Donut - First up is to make a wood donut, which is going to be the main supporting structure for the tube.\n3. Cut Room for Legs - Tripod time!\n4. Notching Your Legs - Cut out three lengths of your 1x2 so that the wood donut will clear the top of the fan, and you'll have a couple inches between your donut and your w…\n5. Screw and Drill - Grab your L-brackets and screw them on so they'll be on the underside of your platform.\n6. Add Wind Tube Supports - Each leg will need a little platform for the wind tube to rest on.\n7. Casters - These rollie-pollies are optional of course.\n8. Making the Tube - Get ready to take 2D plastic into the third dimension.\n9. Prep Tube Attachment - While your tube sits neatly on the wood base, you'll want to attach it there.\n\nLearning Focus: wind, tube, aerodynamics, science, education, teaching\nOriginal Activity: https://www.instructables.com/Wind-Tube/",
