    summary: "Oh what lucky and soon to be glittery friends you have!",
    description: "Overview: Oh what lucky and soon to be glittery friends you have! Get the party popping with a fountain of glitter, all in a game of chance. C'mon, it's only 1 in 6 that YOUR popper is going to be filled with a heaping pile of miniature joy sprinkles that you'll wear for the next month. You'll find it quite easy to do and quite easy to gain or lose friends with it. Let's play! - What: Glitter Roulette! - Concepts: Pure joy, a…\n\nMaterials:\n- See full materials list on the activity page.\n\nBuild Steps:\n1. Safety! - Oh yes, the safety part!\n2. Remove Cardboard Cap - You can remove the cardboard cap pretty easily with a little bit of squeezing of the party popper and getting in there with a fork tine.\n3. Add Glitter - Pick one (or more) party poppers to be the glitter bomb.\n4. Replace Cardboard Cap - You can push that cardboard cap back in to position so it looks like the others.\n5. Glitter Roulette Time! - Pick 5 friends, and have them all choose one.\n6. Why Stop at Glitter? - Okay, so glitter is the best, but when the host can't take it anymore, tThere are so many other fun things to fill party poppers with!\n7. Going Deeper: Inside a Party Popper - If you want to lift up the curtain on the magic, you can check out your party popper.\n\nLearning Focus: glitter, roulette, party trick, prank, primary explosives, party popper\nOriginal Activity: https://www.instructables.com/Glitter-Roulette-with-Party-Poppers/",
