    summary: "Want to go back to your Grateful Dead days, but can't get yourself to order a lava lamp from Hot Topic?",
    description: "Overview: Want to go back to your Grateful Dead days, but can't get yourself to order a lava lamp from Hot Topic? Or maybe you want to introduce kids to the amazing wonders of density as it relates to temperature, and you're looking for an accessible project? Either way, you're in luck, because the water lava lamp not only produces more psychedelic images than you can shake a purple giraffe at, but it also is a wonderful and…\n\nMaterials:\n- See full materials list on the activity page.\n\nBuild Steps:\n1. Ice Ice Baby - For the ice, simply add a lot of food coloring to water in an ice cube tray.\n2. Red Hot! - The red hot is also straightforward.\n3. Watch Your Lava Go! - Have fun as your lava lamp takes action.There are many things to observe beyond the \"hot goes up, cold goes down\" lesson in density.\n\nLearning Focus: density, buoyancy, cold, hot, water, lava\nOriginal Activity: https://www.instructables.com/Water-Lava-Lamp/",
