    title: "Water Drop Trampoline",
    summary: "Water you doing today?",
    description: "Overview: Water you doing today? Add some bounce to your bubble and some dance to your drops with the water drop trampoline! Columns of air moving at different speeds let you float drops in a hovering boogie. We set out to make this as a homemade version of one of our favorite exhibits at the Exploratorium, \"Dancing Drops.\" Now you can have it in your own classroom or home for the cost of almost free. Just the relational cost…\n\nMaterials:\n- See full materials list on the activity page.\n\nBuild Steps:\n1. Skinny Straw Bundle - Grab a bunch o' skinny straws and rubber band them together at the top and bottom.\n2. Fat Straw Wall - Attach a wad of fat straws onto your skinny straw bundle.\n3. Tube Time - Stick your straw bundle in your tube, and if all's right, friction will hold it there.\n4. Blowdryer Taping - First, tape on your straw tube.\n5. Make a Wood Base - There are many ways to make a base, and not all have to be out of wood.\n6. Drill a Hole - Drill a hole that's large enough for your tube to fit through.\n7. Screw It All Together - Huzzah!\n8. Water Bounce Time! - You did it!\n\nLearning Focus: water, drop, fluid, dynamics, aerodynamic, flow\nOriginal Activity: https://www.instructables.com/Water-Drop-Trampoline/",
