    subject: "Science",
    title: "Flower Dissection!",
    summary: "When you get a biologist flowers, they may not stay intact.",
    description: "Overview: When you get a biologist flowers, they may not stay intact. For beautiful things we see every day, there is actually an amazing amount to discover by not only stopping to smell the roses, but look inside them too. In our case, we're going to dissect lilies! Time to put the petal to the metal. - What: Flower Dissection! - Oh, but why: We have to learn somehow - Concepts: biology, botany, anatomy, plant reproduction -…\n\nMaterials:\n- See full materials list on the activity page.\n\nBuild Steps:\n1. Scope Your Flower! - Look at your flower to see how it's all formed.\n2. Petals and Sepals - The outer ring of your flower consists of sepals, and the inner ring is of petals.\n3. The Stamen (male Parts) - Once you peel away the petals and sepals, your flower looks quite a bit more naked.\n4. The Pistil (female Parts) - Well now your flower looks really naked.\n5. Ovary and Nectary - So the ovary is also part of the female parts, but it deserves its own step.\n6. Check Out Some More! - There are so many flowers and so little time!\n\nLearning Focus: flower, dissection, anatomy, biology, botany, pollination\nOriginal Activity: https://www.instructables.com/Flower-Dissection/",
