    title: "Wire Maze!",
    summary: "If you loved the game \"Operation\" as a kid, and want to continue on your path of supreme hand-eye coordination, give this buzzing electronics project a try.",
    description: "Overview: If you loved the game \"Operation\" as a kid, and want to continue on your path of supreme hand-eye coordination, give this buzzing electronics project a try. What's great is you can change the path every time, anywhere from novice post-bac medical school applicant to the manual dexterity of Dr. Octopus. The game is to move the wand from side of the maze to the other without touching the metal wire. If you do, the buz…\n\nMaterials:\n- See full materials list on the activity page.\n\nBuild Steps:\n1. The Posable Wire - Screw in one screw to your baseboard, and wrap your posable wire around it.\n2. Buzzer Electronics! - Test out your buzzer with your battery pack.\n3. Wand Electronics! - Your wand needs wiring, too!\n4. Finishing Touches - Tape a couple inches of both sides of the posable wire.\n5. Play Maze, Change Maze, Repeat! - Keep that arm steady, and good luck not buzzing!\n\nLearning Focus: wire, maze, circuit, electronics, loop, operation\nOriginal Activity: https://www.instructables.com/Wire-Maze/",
