    subject: "STEAM Activity",
    title: "Light Drum!",
    summary: "Light up your life!",
    description: "Overview: Light up your life! Opt in to this optic option with the most wonderful way to introduce kiddos (and adultos) to all of light's tricks. From refracting, diffracting, reflecting, diffusing, the light drum is just wonderful. This is one of our favorite projects for awesome science in the dark. - What: Light Drum! - Where: Your place! - Concepts: Optics, light, reflection, diffraction, refraction, diffusion - Time: ~ 2…\n\nMaterials:\n- See full materials list on the activity page.\n\nBuild Steps:\n1. The Tube - Cut a section from your concrete form tube (anywhere from 9-12\" is good).\n2. The Drum Top - Trace the tube on some wood, and find the center of the circle.\n3. Top Holes - You need a hole for your light, and also some vent holes to keep the whole system cool, and also make it look neat.\n4. Top It Off - Make sure it all fits, and then drill some screws in the sides to make sure the top stays!\n5. Filters - Oh so many fun ways to play with light!\n6. Attach Your Filters - Press on a sample filter, and mark where the drill holes are.\n7. Brad and Repeat! - You have your brads, you have your filters.\n8. Make Fun Optics Things! - Glue up your favorite optics things!\n9. Light It Up! - Turn off the lights, and learn about optics!\n\nLearning Focus: light, optics, diffraction, refraction, diffusion, reflection\nOriginal Activity: https://www.instructables.com/Light-Drum/",
