    title: "Giant Wave Model!",
    summary: "Why hello there, I didn't see you waving!",
    description: "Overview: Why hello there, I didn't see you waving! With your new gargantuan wave model, you'll never have to miss a wave again. Transverse, interference, standing waves, nodes, this lovely science giant has got it all. Put it up in a classroom, at a homemade science museum, or to wow your auntie at the next family reunion. Let's model! - What: Giant Wave Model - Concepts: waves, transverse waves, interference, nodes, periods…\n\nMaterials:\n- See full materials list on the activity page.\n\nBuild Steps:\n1. Get Your Supplies - Gather up those supplies!\n2. Cut the Dowels - First up, cut those dowels!\n3. Measure and Drill Thru-holes - Measure in and mark 3\" or so from each side to make your holes.\n4. Drill Wood Balls - Craft balls!\n5. Make Some Wooden Dumbbells - If you want to feel great about yourself, try lifting these!\n6. Assembly Time! - Time to put them all together!\n7. Cut and Tie Off Both Ends - At the end, tie a not in the strings on both sides to keep everything in place.\n8. Ride the Waves! - Oh snap!\n\nLearning Focus: giant, wave, model, science, education, classroom\nOriginal Activity: https://www.instructables.com/Giant-Wave-Model/",
