    title: "Jurassic Pie!",
    summary: "Welcome to Jurassic Pie.",
    description: "Overview: Welcome to Jurassic Pie. With sixty-five million years in the making, you can't help but fall in lava with it! Truly. You'll have frosting lava all over your kitchen for days, but good gosh was it worth it. If you want to take science to the streets (a cake auction), try out this erupting recipe. - What: Jurassic Pie! (Okay, it's a Volcano cake) - Time: ~ 5 hours - Cost: ~ $40 - Science concepts: eh....joy? - Materi…\n\nMaterials:\n- See full materials list on the activity page.\n\nBuild Steps:\n1. Make Tons of Chocolate Cakes - You're going to be like a mechanical Julia Child in just a second.\n2. Sculpt Your Volcano - Michelangelo time!\n3. Pour Choco Base Layer - Who knew microwaving frosting could look so pretty?\n4. Erupt With Lava Frosting - It's time to fall in lava!\n5. Insert Bottle Lava Chamber - Time for the lava tube!\n6. Add Dinosaurs! - Yay dinosaurs!\n7. Unleash the Eruption! - It's explosion time!\n8. Attempt to Defeat Jurassic Pie - Good luck defeating Jurassic Pie.\n9. Become Dinosaurs and Take Over an Island - Ahhh yes, and if you're feeling extra spunky, throw on some homemade dinosaur suits, take over an island, and get ready for the sequel.\n\nLearning Focus: jurassic, pie, volcano, cake, dry ice, explosion\nOriginal Activity: https://www.instructables.com/Jurassic-Pie-aka-Volcano-Cake/",
