    summary: "If you've been flossing nerdbots, they're about to get their motherboards rearranged by Elasti-Bot: the posable wooden robot who poses, dozes, and is in the know-ses.",
    description: "Overview: If you've been flossing nerdbots, they're about to get their motherboards rearranged by Elasti-Bot: the posable wooden robot who poses, dozes, and is in the know-ses. This gal/guy is a fully posable wood-bot based on a robot we love called CubeBot. Here at Oakland Toy Lab, we of course wanted to make our own. Now you should, too! - What: Elasti-Bot: the posable wooden robot, yo! - Time: ~ 30 minutes - Cost: ~ 50 cen…\n\nMaterials:\n- See full materials list on the activity page.\n\nBuild Steps:\n1. Cut Your Bot-ty Parts - I looked at the CubeBot design, and based our model on that one.\n2. Drill Holes for Elastic - It's hole-drilling time, and there are lots of holes to drill!\n3. Pull Elastic Through and Tie - You're almost there!\n4. Pose and Play! - Oh snap!\n\nLearning Focus: elastic, wood, robot, posable, cubebot, homemade\nOriginal Activity: https://www.instructables.com/Elasti-Bot-the-posable-wooden-robot/",
